pertrophy, autosomal recessive inheritance, biventricular hypertrophy\n  Favours second: abnormal left ventricle morphology, abnormal left ventricular function, fatigue, heart failure, hypoplastic left heart\n\nHypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy (HOCM) vs Brugada Syndrome (Right Bundle Path Block Type):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, autosomal recessive inheritance\n  Favours second: bundle branch block, first degree atrioventricular block, j wave, paroxysmal ventricular tachycardia, presyncope\n\nHypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy (HOCM) vs Long QT Syndrome / Congenital Arrhythmia Syndromes:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, autosomal recessive inheritance\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, coronary artery atherosclerosis, fainting\n\nHypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy (HOCM) vs Catecholaminergic Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia (CPVT):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, arrhythmia, ascites, asymmetric septal hypertrophy, biventricular hypertrophy\n  Favours second: abnormal left ventricular function, atrial standstill, bradycardia, coma, dizziness\n\nArrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia (ARVD) vs Left Ventricular Noncompaction (LVNC):\n  Favours first:  autosomal recessive inheritance, bundle branch block, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia, dyspnea\n  Favours second: abnormal left ventricle morphology, abnormal left ventricular function, arrhythmia, fatigue, heart failure\n\nArrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia (ARVD) vs Brugada Syndrome (Right Bundle Path Block Type):\n  Favours first:  autosomal recessive inheritance, chest pain, congestive heart failure, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia\n  Favours second: cardiac arrest, first degree atrioventricular block, j wave, paroxysmal ventricular tachycardia, prolonged pr interval\n\nArrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia (ARVD) vs Long QT Syndrome / Congenital Arrhythmia Syndromes:\n  Favours first:  autosomal recessive inheritance, bundle branch block, chest pain, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, coronary artery atherosclerosis\n\nArrhythmogenic Right Ventricular Dysplasia (ARVD) vs Catecholaminergic Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia (CPVT):\n  Favours first:  bundle branch block, congestive heart failure, dilatation of the ventricular cavity, dyskinesia, dyspnea\n  Favours second: abnormal left ventricular function, atrial standstill, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, coma\n\nLeft Ventricular Noncompaction (LVNC) vs Brugada Syndrome (Right Bundle Path Block Type):\n  Favours first:  abnormal left ventricle morphology, abnormal left ventricular function, arrhythmia, chest pain, congestive heart failure\n  Favours second: bundle branch block, cardiac arrest, first degree atrioventricular block, j wave, paroxysmal ventricular tachycardia\n\nLeft Ventricular Noncompaction (LVNC) vs Long QT Syndrome / Congenital Arrhythmia Syndromes:\n  Favours first:  abnormal left ventricle morphology, abnormal left ventricular function, arrhythmia, chest pain, fatigue\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, coronary artery atherosclerosis\n\nLeft Ventricular Noncompaction (LVNC) vs Catecholaminergic Polymorphic Ventricular Tachycardia (CPVT):\n  Favours first:  abnormal left ventricle morphology, arrhythmia, congestive heart failure, fatigue, heart failure\n  Favours second: atrial standstill, autosomal recessive inheritance, bradycardia, cardiac arrest, coma\n\nBrugada Syndrome (Right Bundle Path Block Type) vs Long QT Syndrome / Congenital Arrhythmia Syndromes:\n  Favours first:  bundle branch block, first degree atrioventricular block, j wave, paroxysmal ventricular tachycardia, presyncope\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ear, blurred vision, bradycardia, congestive heart failure, coronary artery atherosclerosis"}
