ology, anxiety, chylopericardium, clammy and cold extremities, confusion\n\nRestrictive Cardiomyopathy (Acute) vs Subacute Constrictive Pericarditis (Phase-Transforming to Acute):\n  Favours first:  abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal conjunctiva morphology, abnormal liver parenchyma morphology, abnormal lung morphology, abnormal nasal mucosa morphology\n  Favours second: abnormal pericardium morphology, serositis\n\nRestrictive Cardiomyopathy (Acute) vs Acute Pulmonary Embolism from Proximal Deep Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal conjunctiva morphology, abnormal liver parenchyma morphology, abnormal lung morphology, abnormal nasal mucosa morphology\n  Favours second: clammy skin, coughing up blood, excessive sweating, increased heart rate, leg pain\n\nCardiac Tamponade (Acute) vs Subacute Constrictive Pericarditis (Phase-Transforming to Acute):\n  Favours first:  anxiety, chest pain, chylopericardium, clammy and cold extremities, confusion\n  Favours second: serositis\n\nCardiac Tamponade (Acute) vs Acute Pulmonary Embolism from Proximal Deep Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal pericardium morphology, anxiety, chylopericardium, clammy and cold extremities, confusion\n  Favours second: clammy skin, coughing up blood, dizziness, excessive sweating, fainting\n\nSubacute Constrictive Pericarditis (Phase-Transforming to Acute) vs Acute Pulmonary Embolism from Proximal Deep Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  abnormal pericardium morphology, serositis\n  Favours second: chest pain, clammy skin, coughing up blood, dizziness, excessive sweating\n\nRelated to Restrictive Cardiomyopathy (Acute): dilated cardiomyopathy, endomyocardial fibrosis, familial restrictive cardiomyopathy\n\nRelated to Cardiac Tamponade (Acute): pericardial effusion (disease)\n\nRelated to Subacute Constrictive Pericarditis (Phase-Transforming to Acute): pericarditis (disease)\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55