c metabolic disorder: maternal refusal of prenatal testing and healthy siblings reduce suspicion (de novo variant still a remote possibility)", "Meconium ileus/plug syndrome: weakly opposed by DRE patency, but not definitively ruled out in absence of imaging/pathology (confidence threshold for exclusion <0.3)"], "alarm_features": ["Down syndrome facial dysmorphology (10-20% incidence of Hirschsprung’s disease)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Anatomic GI Obstruction in Neonate", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.2644628099173554, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Digital rectal exam yielding stool/flatulence weakly opposes duodenal atresia as a proximal obstruction would generally prevent distal meconium passage without requiring surgical decompression, though variants with communicating fistula may exhibit this finding."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there evidence of bowel atresia on abdominal imaging?", "Did the physical exam suggest other anatomical anomalies?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Upper gastrointestinal contrast imaging", "Abdominal ultrasound to assess for malrotation or duodenal atresia"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Congenital Enterocolic Dysmotility Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.44628099173553715, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Down syndrome features (upslanting palpebral fissures, single transverse palmar crease) moderately support Hirschsprung disease due to the 10-20% increased incidence 