ary Syndrome", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6666666666666667, "posterior": 0.44594594594594583, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The positional chest pain pattern (worsening supine, improving upright) supports acute pericardial disease, while the absence of ECG findings for STEMI or electrolyte disturbances challenges acute coronary syndrome and cardiac electrolyte abnormalities. Syncope raises suspicion for arrhythmia or infarction over pericarditis."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there any history of chest pain radiation to left arm?", "Are associated symptoms of nausea or diaphoresis present?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG for ST-segment elevation pattern"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathophysiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Structural/Obstructive Cardiac Disease", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06756756756756754, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The positional chest pain pattern (worsening supine, improving upright) supports acute pericardial disease, while the absence of ECG findings for STEMI or electrolyte disturbances challenges acute coronary syndrome and cardiac electrolyte abnormalities. Syncope raises suspicion for arrhythmia or infarction over pericarditis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Pericardial / Acute Inflammatory Cardiac Process", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.14814814814814814, "posterior": 0.04504504504504503, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Upright posture benefiting pain supports pericarditis over STEMI; absence of new Q waves further weakens STEMI likelihood in favor of unstable angina.", "Supine worsening/unupright improvement is highly suggestive of pericarditis and directly contradicts STEMI pathophysiology, though does not exclude NSTEMI or unstable angina."], "evidence_against": ["Syncope challenges pericarditis (classic positional pain without arrhythmia) but lacks strength to definitively favor STEMI, as prolonged QRS absence (evidence E17) weakens STEMI likelihood."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Any ECG findings like diffuse concave ST elevation in multiple leads?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG for pericarditis pattern", "Chest X-ray for pericardial effusion"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "pathophysiology"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Cardiac Electrolyte Abnormality", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03603603603603603, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Diabetes and normotensive ECG reduce hypokalemia suspicion and indirectly favor NSTEMI as a risk factor, given the syncope-angina connection."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (STEMI) with Left Anterior Descending Artery (LAD) Occlusion", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06756756756756756, "danger": 1.0, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Supine worsening/unupright improvement is highly suggestive of pericarditis and directly contradicts STEMI pathophysiology, though does not exclude NSTEMI or unstable angina."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Non-ST Elevation MI (NSTEMI) with Arrhythmogenic Ischemic Injury", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.21621621621621617, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3"